<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Why Age Groups?</h2>

<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">(i) Tight filtering around the target age.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each target (e.g. 15 yr), we re-estimate the biological age of every candidate image with MiVOLO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">60</a>, <a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">58</a>]</cite> and keep only those whose error <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert\hat{Age}-Age_{\text{target}}\rvert\leq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert\hat{Age}-Age_{\text{target}}\rvert\leq 3</annotation></semantics></math> yr, the empirical RMSE of our pipeline.
Thus the so-called “10–20” range in the main text is, in practice, centered tightly on 15.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">(ii) Upper bound given by estimator noise.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">State-of-the-art age estimators, <em id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">e.g.</em>, MiVOLO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">60</a>, <a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">58</a>]</cite>, report a 3.65 yr MAE on in-the-wild faces.
Therefore, even “exact” labels still carry <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq\!3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq\!3</annotation></semantics></math> yr latent noise, limiting the value of pursuing single-year annotation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">(iii) Exact-age ablation.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We repeated fine-tuning under three alternative label settings:
(a) the default <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">age group</span> filtering (±3 yr);
(b) a much smaller subset whose <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ground truth</span> annotation is exactly 15 / 45 / 75 yr;
(c) a subset whose <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">estimated</span> age (via MiVOLO) falls exactly on those targets.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A1.T4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 4</span>: </span><span id="A1.T4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Age errors (<math id="A1.T4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\delta|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\delta|</annotation></semantics></math>, MAE) for age group, GT-exact, and estimator-exact training.</span></figcaption>
<table id="A1.T4.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A1.T4.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T4.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"></th>
<th id="A1.T4.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">age group</th>
<th id="A1.T4.5.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">ground truth</th>
<th id="A1.T4.5.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">estimated</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A1.T4.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T4.5.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">15 <math id="A1.T4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{|\delta|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{|\delta|}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A1.T4.5.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="A1.T4.5.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4.61</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">10.44</td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">7.61</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T4.5.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T4.5.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row">15 MAE</th>
<td id="A1.T4.5.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A1.T4.5.3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4.92</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">10.90</td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center">8.28</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T4.5.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T4.5.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row">45 <math id="A1.T4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{|\delta|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{|\delta|}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A1.T4.5.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">15.87</td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">8.42</td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center"><span id="A1.T4.5.4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">6.69</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T4.5.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T4.5.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row">45 MAE</th>
<td id="A1.T4.5.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">16.90</td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">13.61</td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center"><span id="A1.T4.5.5.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">13.56</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T4.5.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T4.5.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row">75 <math id="A1.T4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{|\delta|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{|\delta|}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A1.T4.5.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">24.10</td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A1.T4.5.6.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">23.03</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.6.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center">26.06</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T4.5.7" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T4.5.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">75 MAE</th>
<td id="A1.T4.5.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="A1.T4.5.7.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">24.14</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">24.86</td>
<td id="A1.T4.5.7.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">26.58</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Tab. <a href="#A1.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ (iii) Exact-age ablation. ‣ Appendix A Why Age Groups? ‣ AgeBooth: Controllable Facial Aging and Rejuvenation via Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> indicates that refining to <em id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">ground-truth</em> 15-yr faces offers virtually no accuracy gain over our age-group baseline, while the subset defined by <em id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">estimated</em> exact ages yields a noticeable improvement only at the 45-yr target; for the other two targets the age-group setting remains superior. Given the negligible benefit at 15 yr, the single-age advantage limited to 45 yr, and the substantially higher curation cost of assembling exact-age subsets, we retain the age-group strategy as the most cost-effective choice.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">These results confirm that age groups strike a better balance between annotation effort and performance.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Continuity of the SVDMix</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section establishes that the fused LoRA weight <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\theta_{\text{fused}}(\alpha)\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>fused</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\theta_{\text{fused}}(\alpha)\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> obtained with the SVD - based fusion strategy is a <em id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">continuous</em> function of the blending coefficient <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\text{young}},B_{\text{old}}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mtext>young</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\text{young}},B_{\text{old}}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\text{young}},A_{\text{old}}\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mtext>young</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\text{young}},A_{\text{old}}\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\ll\min\{m,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≪</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\ll\min\{m,n\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For each <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ast\in\{\text{young},\text{old}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext>young</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>old</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ast\in\{\text{young},\text{old}\}</annotation></semantics></math> we write the thin singular value decomposition (SVD) as</p>
<table id="A2.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\ast}=U_{\ast}\Sigma_{\ast}V_{\ast}^{\!\top},\quad A_{\ast}=P_{\ast}\Lambda_{\ast}Q_{\ast}^{\!\top}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\ast}=U_{\ast}\Sigma_{\ast}V_{\ast}^{\!\top},\quad A_{\ast}=P_{\ast}\Lambda_{\ast}Q_{\ast}^{\!\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where the factors have the usual orthogonality and diagonality properties.
For a given <math id="A2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> we define the SVDMix operator by linearly blending the factors:</p>
<table id="A2.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{\alpha}=\alpha U_{\text{young}}+(1-\alpha)U_{\text{old}},\quad\text{etc.}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mtext>young</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>etc.</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{\alpha}=\alpha U_{\text{young}}+(1-\alpha)U_{\text{old}},\quad\text{etc.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">and set</p>
<table id="A2.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\text{fused}}(\alpha)=U_{\alpha}\Sigma_{\alpha}V_{\alpha}^{\!\top},\qquad A_{\text{fused}}(\alpha)=P_{\alpha}\Lambda_{\alpha}Q_{\alpha}^{\!\top}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mtext>fused</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mtext>fused</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\text{fused}}(\alpha)=U_{\alpha}\Sigma_{\alpha}V_{\alpha}^{\!\top},\qquad A_{\text{fused}}(\alpha)=P_{\alpha}\Lambda_{\alpha}Q_{\alpha}^{\!\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">The final weight update used by the diffusion model is</p>
<table id="A2.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\theta_{\text{fused}}(\alpha)=B_{\text{fused}}(\alpha)\,A_{\text{fused}}(\alpha)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>fused</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mtext>fused</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mtext>fused</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\theta_{\text{fused}}(\alpha)=B_{\text{fused}}(\alpha)\,A_{\text{fused}}(\alpha).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We denote by <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{\mathrm{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{\mathrm{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> the Frobenius norm and
recall two elementary facts:
(i) every matrix entry obtained from linear interpolation(Eq. <a href="#A2.E14" title="In Appendix B Continuity of the SVDMix ‣ AgeBooth: Controllable Facial Aging and Rejuvenation via Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>) is an <em id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">affine</em> function of <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, hence continuous;
(ii) matrix addition and multiplication are linear and therefore continuous with respect to the
Frobenius norm.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The mapping
<math id="A2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:[0,1]\to\mathbb{R}^{m\times n},\;\alpha\mapsto\Delta\theta_{\emph{fused}}(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:[0,1]\to\mathbb{R}^{m\times n},\;\alpha\mapsto\Delta\theta_{\emph{fused}}(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>
defined in (<a href="#A2.E16" title="In Appendix B Continuity of the SVDMix ‣ AgeBooth: Controllable Facial Aging and Rejuvenation via Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>)
is continuous on the closed interval <math id="A2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Fix any <math id="A2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{0}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{0}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\alpha_{k}\}\subset[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\alpha_{k}\}\subset[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> be
a sequence with <math id="A2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{k}\to\alpha_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{k}\to\alpha_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Because each entry of the blended factors
<math id="A2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{\alpha},\Sigma_{\alpha},V_{\alpha},P_{\alpha},\Lambda_{\alpha},Q_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{\alpha},\Sigma_{\alpha},V_{\alpha},P_{\alpha},\Lambda_{\alpha},Q_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>
is an affine (hence continuous) function of <math id="A2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>,
we have</p>
<table id="A2.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="U_{\alpha_{k}}\!\xrightarrow[k\to\infty]{}U_{\alpha_{0}},\quad\Sigma_{\alpha_{k}}\!\xrightarrow[k\to\infty]{}\Sigma_{\alpha_{0}},\quad\text{etc.}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo>→</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mphantom></mphantom></munderover><mi>U</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo>→</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mphantom></mphantom></munderover><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>etc.</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{\alpha_{k}}\!\xrightarrow[k\to\infty]{}U_{\alpha_{0}},\quad\Sigma_{\alpha_{k}}\!\xrightarrow[k\to\infty]{}\Sigma_{\alpha_{0}},\quad\text{etc.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">in the entry-wise (and thus Frobenius) sense.
By continuity of matrix multiplication,</p>
<table id="A2.E18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E18X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E18X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B_{\text{fused}}(\alpha_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mtext>fused</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B_{\text{fused}}(\alpha_{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E18X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=U_{\alpha_{k}}\Sigma_{\alpha_{k}}V_{\alpha_{k}}^{\!\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=U_{\alpha_{k}}\Sigma_{\alpha_{k}}V_{\alpha_{k}}^{\!\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E18Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E18Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\xrightarrow[k\to\infty]{}U_{\alpha_{0}}\Sigma_{\alpha_{0}}V_{\alpha_{0}}^{\!\top}\;=\;B_{\text{fused}}(\alpha_{0})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo>→</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mphantom></mphantom></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mtext>fused</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\xrightarrow[k\to\infty]{}U_{\alpha_{0}}\Sigma_{\alpha_{0}}V_{\alpha_{0}}^{\!\top}\;=\;B_{\text{fused}}(\alpha_{0}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p5.3" class="ltx_p">The same holds for <math id="A2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\text{fused}}(\alpha_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mtext>fused</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\text{fused}}(\alpha_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Finally, using bilinearity of the matrix product,</p>
<table id="A2.E19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E19X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E19X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta\theta_{\text{fused}}(\alpha_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>fused</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta\theta_{\text{fused}}(\alpha_{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E19X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=B_{\text{fused}}(\alpha_{k})\,A_{\text{fused}}(\alpha_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mtext>fused</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mtext>fused</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=B_{\text{fused}}(\alpha_{k})\,A_{\text{fused}}(\alpha_{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E19Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E19Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\xrightarrow[k\to\infty]{}B_{\text{fused}}(\alpha_{0})\,A_{\text{fused}}(\alpha_{0})\;=\;\Delta\theta_{\text{fused}}(\alpha_{0})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo>→</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mphantom></mphantom></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mtext>fused</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mtext>fused</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>fused</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\xrightarrow[k\to\infty]{}B_{\text{fused}}(\alpha_{0})\,A_{\text{fused}}(\alpha_{0})\;=\;\Delta\theta_{\text{fused}}(\alpha_{0}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p5.4" class="ltx_p">Hence <math id="A2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is sequentially continuous, which on a
metric space implies continuity.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Because network weights vary continuously with <math id="A2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, the diffusion model’s output varies smoothly as the target age parameter is swept.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Sensitivity Experiment</h2>

<figure id="A3.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.05715v1/sensitivity.png" id="A3.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:429/136;" width="429" height="136" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>: </span><span id="A3.F5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Sensitivity experiment.<span id="A3.F5.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> We vary training size <math id="A3.F5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\in\{1,5,10,20,50\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\in\{1,5,10,20,50\}</annotation></semantics></math> to assess data dependence. Identity drift is evident when <math id="A3.F5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\leq 5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\leq 5</annotation></semantics></math>, but stabilizes for <math id="A3.F5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq 10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq 10</annotation></semantics></math>.
</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To investigate the appropriate amount of training data, we conducted a sensitivity analysis for both small (<math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N&lt;10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N&lt;10</annotation></semantics></math>) and larger values of <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>.
Specifically, we experimented with <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\in\{1,5,10,20,50\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\in\{1,5,10,20,50\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The smaller datasets were strict subsets of the larger ones to eliminate discrepancies due to data inconsistency.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A3.T5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 5</span>: </span><span id="A3.T5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Sensitivity experiment metrics. MAE and age deviation at target ages 15 and 75 across different <math id="A3.T5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
